In (NG)EN-DC, if the UE is unable to comply with part of the configuration in an RRCReconfiguration received over SRB3 and MCG transmission is not suspended, the UE shall:

- initiate the SCG failure information procedure as specified in clause 5.7.3 to report SCG reconfiguration error, upon which the connection reconfiguration procedure ends;  
- initiate the connection re-establishment procedure as specified in TS 36.331, clause 5.3.7, upon which the connection reconfiguration procedure ends.

A UE may initiate transmission of the SidelinkUEInformationNR message to indicate it no longer requires NR sidelink relay discovery announcements resources if:

- The UE is configured by upper layer to transmit NR sidelink L2 U2N relay discovery announcements on a frequency included in sl-FreqInfoList in SIB12 of the PCell including sl-L2U2N-Relay, or configured to transmit NR sidelink L3 U2N relay discovery announcements on a frequency included in sl-FreqInfoList in SIB12 of the PCell including sl-L3U2N-RelayDiscovery;  
- And the last transmission of the SidelinkUEInformationNR message included sl-TxResourceReqListDisc;  
- And the UE has not transmitted a SidelinkUEInformationNR message since the last time it connected to a PCell providing SIB12 including sl-ConfigCommonNR (and the relevant relay discovery feature, e.g., sl-L2U2N-Relay or sl-L3U2N-RelayDiscovery);  
- And the UE is (capable of) acting as U2N Relay UE, and SIB12 includes sl-RelayUE-ConfigCommon, and the U2N Relay UE threshold conditions as specified in 5.8.14.2 are met; or  
- And the UE is selecting a U2N Relay UE / has a selected U2N Relay UE, and SIB12 includes sl-RemoteUE-ConfigCommon, and the U2N Remote UE threshold conditions as specified in 5.8.15.2 are met.

In such cases, the UE shall initiate transmission of the SidelinkUEInformationNR message to indicate it no longer requires NR sidelink relay discovery announcements resources in accordance with 5.8.3.3.

Upon reception of RRCReject, the UE shall:

- Stop timer T300, if running;  
- Stop timer T319, if running;  
- Stop timer T319a, if running;  
- Stop timer T302, if running;  
- Reset MAC and release the default MAC Cell Group configuration;  
- If waitTime is configured in the RRCReject: start timer T302 with the timer value set to waitTime;  
- If RRCReject is received in response to a request from upper layers: inform the upper layer that access barring is applicable for all access categories except categories '0' and '2';  
- If RRCReject is received in response to an RRCSetupRequest: inform upper layers about the failure to setup the RRC connection, upon which the procedure ends;  
- If RRCReject is received in response to an RRCResumeRequest or an RRCResumeRequest1:  
  - If resume is triggered by upper layers: inform upper layers about the failure to resume the RRC connection;  
  - If resume is triggered due to an RNA update or for SDT and T380 is not running:  
    - Set the variable pendingRNA-Update to true;  
    - Discard the current K key, the K key, the K key, the K key and the K key derived in gNB RRCenc RRCint UPint UPenc accordance with 5.3.13.3;  
    - Suspend SRB1 and the radio bearers configured for SDT, if any;  
    - For each radio bearer configured for SDT:  
      - Indicate PDCP suspend to lower layers;  
      - Re-establish the RLC entity as specified in TS 38.322;  
    - The procedure ends;  
- Upon L2 U2N Relay UE receiving RRCReject: either trigger PC5-S release or send Notification message to the connected L2 U2N Remote UE(s) in accordance with 5.8.9.10;  
- The RRC_INACTIVE UE shall continue to monitor paging while timer T302 is running.

For each measObjectId included in the received measObjectToRemoveList that is part of measObjectList in VarMeasConfig, the UE shall:

- remove the entry with the matching measObjectId from the measObjectList within the VarMeasConfig;
- remove all measId associated with this measObjectId from the measIdList within the VarMeasConfig, if any;
- if a measId is removed from the measIdList:
  - remove the measurement reporting entry for this measId from the VarMeasReportList, if included;
  - stop the periodical reporting timer or timer T321 or timer T322, whichever is running, and reset the associated information (e.g. timeToTrigger) for this measId.

For each condReconfigId received in the condReconfigToAddModList IE, the UE shall:

1. If an entry with the matching condReconfigId exists in the condReconfigToAddModList within the VarConditionalReconfig:
   - If the entry includes an condExecutionCond or condExecutionCondSCG, replace condExecutionCond or condExecutionCondSCG within the VarConditionalReconfig with the value received for this condReconfigId;
   - If the entry includes an condRRCReconfig, replace condRRCReconfig within the VarConditionalReconfig with the value received for this condReconfigId;
   - Add a new entry for this condReconfigId within the VarConditionalReconfig;
2. Perform conditional reconfiguration evaluation as specified in 5.3.5.13.4.

Upon reception of RRCReject, the UE shall:

- Stop timer T300, if running;
- Stop timer T319, if running;
- Stop timer T319a, if running;
- Stop timer T302, if running;
- Reset MAC and release the default MAC Cell Group configuration;
- If waitTime is configured in the RRCReject: start timer T302 with the timer value set to the waitTime;
- If RRCReject is received in response to a request from upper layers: inform the upper layer that access barring is applicable for all access categories except categories '0' and '2';
- If RRCReject is received in response to an RRCSetupRequest: inform upper layers about the failure to setup the RRC connection, upon which the procedure ends;
- Else if RRCReject is received in response to an RRCResumeRequest or an RRCResumeRequest1:
  - If resume is triggered by upper layers: inform upper layers about the failure to resume the RRC connection;
  - If resume is triggered due to an RNA update, or if resume is triggered for SDT and T380 is not running: set the variable pendingRNA-Update to true;
  - Discard the current K key, the K key, the K key, the K key and the K key derived in gNB RRCenc RRCint UPint UPenc accordance with 5.3.13.3;
  - Suspend SRB1 and the radio bearers configured for SDT, if any;
  - For each radio bearer configured for SDT: indicate PDCP suspend to lower layers and re-establish the RLC entity as specified in TS 38.322;
  - The procedure ends.

Additionally, if the UE is a L2 U2N Relay UE, it either triggers PC5-S release or sends a Notification message to the connected L2 U2N Remote UE(s) in accordance with 5.8.9.10.

The RRC_INACTIVE UE shall continue to monitor paging while timer T302 is running.

If the upper layer provides NAS PDU, the UE sets the `dedicatedNAS-Message` in the RRC message to include the information received from upper layers.

This is explicitly stated in the first context excerpt:
> 2 > set the dedicatedNAS-Message to include the information received from upper layers;

For each reportConfigId included in the received reportConfigToRemoveList that is part of the current UE configuration in VarMeasConfig, the UE shall:

- Remove the entry with the matching reportConfigId from the reportConfigList within the VarMeasConfig;
- Remove all measId associated with the reportConfigId from the measIdList within the VarMeasConfig, if any;
- If a measId is removed from the measIdList:
  - Remove the measurement reporting entry for this measId from the VarMeasReportList, if included;
  - Stop the periodical reporting timer or timer T321 or timer T322, whichever one is running, and reset the associated information (e.g. timeToTrigger) for this measId.

For each logicalChannelIdentity/LogicalChannelIdentityExt value included in the rlc-BearerToReleaseList/rlc-BearerToReleaseListExt that is part of the current UE configuration within the same cell group, the UE shall:

- release the RLC entity or entities as specified in TS 38.322, clause 5.1.3;
- release the corresponding logical channel.

The UE shall:  
2 > stop T390 for all access categories;  
2 > perform the actions as specified in 5.3.14.4.

The UE shall:  
2 > stop T390 for all access categories;  
2 > perform the actions as specified in 5.3.14.4.

For a periodical report on an E-UTRA cell where rsrp is set to true, the sorting quantity is RSRP.

This is derived from the context:  
> 1 > if the reportType is set to periodical:  
> 2 > determine the sorting quantity according to reportQuantity for an E-UTRA cell, as below:  
> 3 > if a single quantity is set to true:  
> 4 > consider this quantity as the sorting quantity;  
> 4 > if rsrp is set to true;  
> 5 > consider RSRP as the sorting quantity;

If the RRCReestablishment message includes the sl-L2RemoteUEConfig (i.e., the UE is a L2 U2N Remote UE), the UE shall:

- Perform the L2 U2N Remote UE configuration procedure as specified in 5.3.5.16;
- Consider the current cell to be the PCell.

Upon T311 expiry, if the procedure was initiated due to radio link failure or handover failure, the UE shall:

- Set the `noSuitableCellFound` in the `VarRLF-Report` to `true`;
- Perform the actions upon going to RRC_IDLE as specified in 5.3.11, with release cause 'RRC connection failure'.

For each sl-ReportConfigId included in the received sl-ReportConfigToRemoveList that is part of the current UE configuration in VarMeasConfigSL, the UE shall:

- Remove the entry with the matching sl-ReportConfigId from the sl-ReportConfigList within the VarMeasConfigSL;
- Remove all sl-MeasId associated with the sl-ReportConfigId from the sl-MeasIdList within the VarMeasConfigSL, if any;
- If a sl-MeasId is removed from the sl-MeasIdList:
  - Remove the measurement reporting entry for this sl-MeasId from the VarMeasReportListSL, if included;
  - Stop the periodical reporting timer and reset the associated information (e.g. sl-TimeToTrigger) for this sl-MeasId.

When conditions for initiating SDT in accordance with 5.3.13.1b are fulfilled, the UE:

- Considers the resume procedure as initiated for SDT;
- Starts timer T319a;
- Starts timer T319;
- Instructs the MAC entity to consider the cg-SDT-TimeAlignmentTimer as expired, if it is running.

A UE in (NG)EN-DC executes a subclause of clause 5 in this specification when:

- the subclause is referred to from a subclause under execution, either in this specification or in TS 36.331;  
- or the subclause applies to a message received on SRB3 (if SRB3 is established);  
- or the subclause applies to field(s), IE(s), UE variable(s) or timer(s) in this specification that the UE is configured with.

If T304 of the MCG expires and any DAPS bearer is configured without radio link failure detected in the source PCell, the UE shall:

- reset MAC for the target PCell and release the MAC configuration for the target PCell;
- for each DAPS bearer:
  - release the RLC entity or entities as specified in TS 38.322, clause 5.1.3, and the associated logical channel for the target PCell;
  - reconfigure the PDCP entity to release DAPS as specified in TS 38.323;
- release the physical channel configuration for the target PCell;
- discard the keys used in the target PCell (the K key, the K key, the K key, the K key and the gNB RRCenc RRCint UPint K key), if any;
- resume suspended SRBs in the source PCell;
- revert back to the UE configuration used for the DRB or multicast MRB in the source PCell, including PDCP, RLC state variables, the security configuration and the data stored in transmission and reception buffers in PDCP and RLC entities;
- revert back to the UE measurement configuration used in the source PCell;
- store the handover failure information in VarRLF-Report as described in clause 5.3.10.5;
- initiate the failure information procedure as specified in clause 5.7.5 to report DAPS handover failure.

The UE shall consider an MBS service to be part of the MBS services of interest if the following conditions are met:  
1. the UE is receiving or interested to receive this service via a broadcast MRB;  
2. the session of this service is ongoing or about to start;  
3. one or more MBS FSAIs in the USD for this service is included in SIB21 acquired from the PCell for a frequency belonging to the set of MBS frequencies of interest, determined according to 5.9.4.3.

The Sidelink RRC reconfiguration procedure modifies the following:

- Establishment, modification, or release of sidelink DRBs (Data Radio Bearers) associated with a peer UE;
- (Re-)configuration of NR sidelink measurement and reporting;
- (Re-)configuration of sidelink CSI reference signal resources and CSI reporting latency bound;
- (Re-)configuration of the peer UE to perform NR sidelink measurement and report;
- (Re-)configuration of the peer UE to perform sidelink DRX (Discontinuous Reception);
- Release or establishment of PC5 Relay RLC channels for L2 U2N Relay UE and Remote UE;
- Modification of parameters in SL-RLC-ChannelConfig-PC5 for PC5 Relay RLC channels;
- (Re-)configuration of sidelink DRX assistance information;
- Reporting of DRX configuration reject information (when applicable);
- Reporting of parameters related to U2N relay operation.

These modifications are performed via the RRCReconfigurationSidelink message and apply to sidelink communications in NR V2X (Vehicle-to-Everything) scenarios.

If the current configuration contains a BH RLC Channel with the received bh-RLC-ChannelID within the same cell group, the IAB-node shall:

- if reestablishRLC is received: re-establish the RLC entity as specified in TS 38.322;
- reconfigure the RLC entity or entities in accordance with the received rlc-Config;
- reconfigure the logical channel in accordance with the received mac-LogicalChannelConfig.

The UE shall:  
- stop timer T331;  
- perform the actions as specified in 5.7.8.3, upon which the procedure ends.

For each DAPS bearer, when the RRCReconfiguration includes `daps-SourceRelease`, the UE shall:

- Release the RLC entity or entities as specified in TS 38.322, clause 5.1.3, and the associated logical channel for the source SpCell;
- Reconfigure the PDCP entity to release DAPS as specified in TS 38.323.

When the RRCReconfiguration includes `daps-SourceRelease`, the UE shall:

- Reset the source MAC and release the source MAC configuration;
- For each DAPS bearer:
  - Release the RLC entity or entities as specified in TS 38.322, clause 5.1.3, and the associated logical channel for the source SpCell;
  - Reconfigure the PDCP entity to release DAPS as specified in TS 38.323;
- For each SRB:
  - Release the PDCP entity for the source SpCell;
  - Release the RLC entity as specified in TS 38.322, clause 5.1.3, and the associated logical channel for the source SpCell;
- Release the physical channel configuration for the source SpCell;
- Discard the keys used in the source SpCell (the K_eNB, K_gNB, K_RRCenc, K_RRCint, K_UPenc, and K_UPint keys), if any.

The UE shall:
- derive or update the secondary key (S-K or S-KeNB) based on the KgNB key and using the received sk-Counter value, as specified in TS 33.501;
- derive the K key and the K key as specified in TS 33.501 using the ciphering algorithms indicated in the RadioBearerConfig associated with the secondary key (S-K or S-KeNB) as indicated by keyToUse;
- derive the K key and the K key as specified in TS 33.501 using the integrity protection algorithms indicated in the RadioBearerConfig associated with the secondary key (S-K or S-KeNB) as indicated by keyToUse.

The UE includes the mobilityState in the RRCSetupComplete message when the RRCSetup is received in response to an RRCSetupRequest **if speedStateReselectionPars is configured in the SIB2**.

This is derived from the following statement in the context:
> 2 &gt; if the RRCSetup is received in response to an RRCResumeRequest, RRCResumeRequest1 or RRCSetupRequest: 3 &gt; if speedStateReselectionPars is configured in the SIB2: 4 &gt; include the mobilityState in the RRCSetupComplete message and set it to the mobility state (as specified in TS 38.304 ) of the UE just prior to entering RRC_CONNECTED state;

If the targetRAT-Type in the MobilityFromNRCommand is set to utra-fdd, the UE shall:

- Consider inter-RAT mobility as initiated towards UTRA-FDD;
- Forward the nas-SecurityParamFromNR to the upper layers, if included;
- Access the target cell indicated in the inter-RAT message in accordance with the specifications of the target RAT.
